#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0125.1 expect=noViolation domain=SE
#note "The unplanned element IS described, so the sheet Rule (SEUPDES ^= null) is satisfied; row 2 is planned and outside the Condition. Silent before AND after M3-D3 -- before for the wrong reason (the spurious var_exists(\"UNPLAN\") guard), after for the right one -- which is exactly why it cannot substitute for the invalid fixture."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset SE label="Subject Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col SEUPDES type=Char label="Description of Unplanned Element"
---
S1 | SE | SUBJ-001 | 1 | UNPLAN | Extra dosing visit
S1 | SE | SUBJ-001 | 2 | SCRN   |
---
